 "texts": [
  "PRODUCTION BRIEF",
  "Sawt al-Nahr — Documentary Series",
  "Season 2  ·  Episodes 04–06  ·  Draft 3.1  ·  Revised 12 May 2026",
  "Director",
  "Karim Fahmy  —  Premiere Pro 2026 / DaVinci Resolve 20",
  "Delivery",
  "3 × 26 min  ·  UHD 3840×2160  ·  25 fps  ·  Rec.709",
  "1. Project Overview",
  "1.1 Objectives",
  "1.2 Deliverables",
  "2. Technical Specifications",
  "3. Schedule",
  "4. Contacts",
  "Appendix A — Shot List, Episode 04",
  "Sawt al-Nahr follows three families whose livelihoods depend on the Nile between Aswan and Rosetta. Episodes 04–06 move the series from portraiture into argument: each cut should carry one clear question and answer it with images before anyone speaks. The offline edit is built in Premiere Pro; the conform, grade and deliverables happen in DaVinci Resolve.",
  "Hold the audience through a six-minute cold open with no narration.",
  "Keep archive material under 20% of running time.",
  "Prefer 1970s 16 mm over broadcast news where both exist.",
  "Deliver a clean textless master alongside every subtitled version.",
  "Broadcast master, per the specification in",
  "Section 2",
  "Web cut with burned-in Arabic subtitles.",
  "Vertical 9:16 trailer, 45 seconds, for social.",
  "Six still frames at full resolution for press.",
  "Archive package: project files, LUTs, and a bin-by-bin media report.",
  "“Cut on the movement, not on the word.”",
  "All versions are graded from the same Rec.709 timeline. Anything",
  "underlined",
  "struck through",
  "highlighted",
  "below marks a change since draft 2.9. Frame rate is 25p",
  "; timecode starts at 10:00:00:00.",
  "All versions",
  "ProRes 422 HQ",
  "H.264, 24 Mb/s",
  "WAV 48 kHz / 24-bit",
  "−23 LUFS",
  "−16 LUFS",
  "True peak ≤ −1 dBTP",
  "SRT + burned-in",
  "Table 1 — Delivery specification by version",
  "Figure 1 — Calibration strip shipped at the head of every master",
  "Dates below are hard for the picture lock and soft for everything upstream of it. If an interview slips, the assembly absorbs it; the lock does not move.",
